A '''Mandalorian covert''' was located on the [[space station]] [[Glavis Ringworld]] during the [[New Republic Era]]. After the [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|Mandalorian covert]] on [[Nevarro]] was exposed and [[Attack on the Tribe|massacred]] by [[Moff]] [[Gideon's Imperial remnant]], two survivors of [[the Tribe]], [[the Armorer]] and [[Paz Vizsla]], established the new [[covert]]. [[Din Djarin]] later joined and helped them, but was banished after he revealed that he had removed his helmet, which was against the strict rules of the [[Way of the Mandalore]] followed by the [[Children of the Watch]]. The Armorer and Vizsla later relocated to another [[Mandalorian secret covert|covert]].

==Description==
This [[Mandalorian]] [[covert]] was located in the lower sublevels of the [[space station]] [[Glavis Ringworld]], near [[Kolzoc Alley]], and was accessible through a secret door with a camouflaged [[mythosaur]] symbol on it, viewable only through a [[macrobinocular viewplate]]. Its main feature was a [[cryo-furnace]], which was placed on an elevated platform next to a service corridor open to the vacuum of space. A cabinet of forgery tools, such as a [[gravity hammer]] and [[magnetic tongs]], was located right next to the [[forge]].<ref name="Return" />

==History==
===Prelude===
Following the exposure of the [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|Mandalorian covert]] on [[Nevarro]] and the [[attack on the Tribe]] by [[Moff]] [[Gideon's Imperial remnant]],<ref name="Redemption">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> [[Paz Vizsla]] and [[the Armorer]] were able to escape and reach Glavis. They established a hiding place in the lower sublevels of the ring world, next to the heat exhaust towers. They left signs leading to their new covert along Glavis Ringworld's Kolzoc Alley that were visible to vision settings in a Mandalorian's helmet.<ref name="Return" />

===Establishment of the Covert===
Paz Vizsla and the Armorer were soon joined by bounty hunter [[Din Djarin]] who had discovered the location of the covert using information by [[Ishi Tib]]. Djarin was welcomed by the Armorer, and after presenting her with the [[Darksaber]] he assisted her and Paz Vizsla with the establishment of the covert, by setting up the [[beskar]] forge and the forgery cabinet. Djarin also presented to them the [[beskar spear]] he obtained by [[Ahsoka Tano]], but was forced to melt it by the Armorer who stated that it is a dangerous weapon as it can pierce beskar armor. The spear was reforged into an [[Grogu's chainmail shirt|armor]] for [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] by Djarin's request. As she was melting the spear, the Armorer recounted to Djarin the history of the Darksaber and the [[Night of a Thousand Tears]].<ref name="Return" />

===Duel on the bridge===
Following Djarin's arrival at the covert, he began training with the Darksaber, as instructed by the Armorer, in a service bridge above the vacuum of space. However, due to his struggling, he was declared unworthy of wielding it by Paz Vizsla, who soon challenged him to a [[Fight for the Darksaber|duel]] for the saber. Din accepted the challenge, and fought Vizsla who was armed with a [[Personal Combat Shield]] and a [[vibroblade]], and was initially disarmed, but soon gained the upper hand, and the Armorer concluded the duel over, with Djarin being the winner. However, the Armorer asked them if they removed their helmets, and Djarin admitted that he did, and was then banished as a punishment, unless he could atone in the [[Living Waters]] beneath the [[Mines of Mandalore]], as per the [[Way of the Mandalore]]. Djarin left the covert, the Darksaber still at his possesion.<ref name="Return" />

===Leaving the covert===
At some point later, the Armorer and Vizsla relocated to another [[Mandalorian secret covert|covert]] on a [[Armorer's planet|desert planet]], where they were joined by more Mandalorians<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref> from the Tribe.<ref name="Chapter 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref>

